# Default Runlevel

### Checking the Default Runlevel
Check the `inittab` file
example
<img src="../../../Image/checkingrunlevel.png" style="width:40%; border:1px solid lightgrey">
<span>&nbsp;</span>

### Changing the Default Runlevel
Edit the **initdefault** line in `/etc/inittab`
if the system doesn't have that file, create one with only an **initdefault** line that specifies the default runlevel
<span>&nbsp;</span>

### Checking Current Runlevel
`runlevel`
<img src="../../../Image/runlevel.png" style="width:15%; border:1px solid lightgrey">
**N** → means system hasn't switched runlevels since booting
<span>&nbsp;</span>

